Having a pretty good game.  Mines dealt with, Sokoban dealt with
(almost - two pets died in the zoo and I had left it for a later
cleanup), co-aligned Priest in Minetown, taking good care of myself and
playing low-risk.  So I thought.

Just when I'm on my way back to the main dungeon to look for things
like a bag of holding, sorely needed at this stage, my weapon gets
nicked by a mountain nymph.  And part of my armour gets nicked by a
water nymph.  I go chasing them, meeting one in a room east of Minetown
proper - zap zap and it's dead.  Weapon recovered.

Down a corridor, and there's the other one.  Start throwing daggers
(expert I am), but the nymph starts reading scrolls of earth (which it
stole from my altar).  I kill the nymph, but I'm bouldered-in, so I go
the wand of digging.  Needs more than one zap.  Izchak's voice thunders
through the dungeon!  "Who dared drill into my shop?"

WTF?  Why does a wand of digging suddenly extend 15 squares?

So I eventually push the boulders aside to make a retreat - I can see
Izchak coming - but I get cornered by the Watch Captain (whom I could
swear was killed by my cat about 2000 turns ago) and another guard.  I
beat a retreat, but there's only one way around the rooms to get back
to the stairs and off this level (and I'm running low on HP and dare
not pray because I used that to make holy water just minutes ago).
Zap, zap, bounce.  Izchak comes and takes all your possessions.
DYWTSWYHWYD?

I had the option of firing a wand of death at Izchak, but I didn't want
to destroy my luck any further during the New Moon period.  Yes, I
would have enjoyed reflection at this point

It was the nymphs' fault.  Delete them from the story and I am still
cruising, on my way to see what was below Dlvl 11.

